---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "AI Workflow Consulting",
  "serviceType": "AI Consulting",
  "provider": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pravine Manivannan", "url": "https://pravinemani.com/" },
  "areaServed": "Worldwide",
  "description": "Production-grade AI workflows, custom MCP servers, agent systems, and prompt and eval suites. Built code-first on Claude Code and Vercel.",
  "url": "https://pravinemani.com/services/ai/"
};
---

<Base title="AI Workflow Consulting · Claude Code, MCP, Agents · Pravine Mani" description="Production AI workflows, custom MCP servers, agent systems and eval suites. Built code-first on Claude Code and Vercel. Toronto consultancy." jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/services/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">services</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <span class="you">ai</span>
  </div>
  <h1>AI workflows,<br><span class="accent">production-grade and code-first.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">AI workflows shipped on a code-first stack: Claude Code, Vercel cron, MCP servers and Supabase. No n8n, no Make, no platform fee.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a href="/services/" class="cta-btn secondary">All engagement shapes</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-grid">

    <article class="vert-card" id="workflows">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">01</span><h2>Workflow automation</h2></div>
      <p>The repetitive work your team does over and over, lead routing, inbox triage, daily briefings, competitor watching and weekly reporting, turned into automations that run on schedule. Written as real code in your repo, not glued together in Zapier.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Automations run on infrastructure you already own, with no extra subscriptions to pay for</li>
        <li>Structured, validated outputs, so downstream systems don't break on unexpected data</li>
        <li>You own the code at the end: versioned in git, debuggable and modifiable</li>
        <li>Two weeks of post-launch support to catch anything the eval suite missed</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="mcp">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">02</span><h2>Custom MCP servers</h2></div>
      <p>An MCP server gives Claude direct access to your data, CRM, database and internal APIs as first-class actions, with no copy-pasting context into a chat window. The AI calls your systems the way a teammate would.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your APIs, database queries and internal tools exposed as actions the AI can take safely</li>
        <li>Every external request signed and verified, so nothing untrusted reaches your data</li>
        <li>A reusable template repository handed off so your team can extend the server without me</li>
        <li>Optional Claude Code skills bundled in, so anyone on your team can install the workflow with one CLI command</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="agents">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">03</span><h2>Agent systems</h2></div>
      <p>A coordinated set of AI agents that handle multi-step work, research, planning, execution and review, with cost limits, error recovery and visibility into every decision. This is the part most teams demo and never get past the demo.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Specialized agents that hand work to each other instead of one bloated mega-prompt</li>
        <li>Hard cost ceilings per task and per user, so a runaway loop can't blow your API bill</li>
        <li>Production observability so you can see what each agent did, why, and what it cost</li>
        <li>For deeper concurrency work, see <a href="/services/agentic-os/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Agentic OS</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="evals">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">04</span><h2>Prompt + eval suites</h2></div>
      <p>A test suite for your AI features: real inputs, expected outputs, scored automatically on every code change. It's the difference between "the demo worked" and "we shipped this to customers and it stayed working." Most teams skip it, which is why AI features regress in production.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>30 to 100 real test cases written from your actual product traffic, not invented</li>
        <li>Every code change runs the suite; if quality drops, the deploy is blocked automatically</li>
        <li>Prompts treated like code: versioned, reviewable and rolled back when needed</li>
        <li>You leave with a real test harness you can extend, not a one-off demo</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="title-block">
      <div class="label">how it works</div>
      <h2>Engagement shapes for AI work.</h2>
      <p>The same paid engagement shapes apply across every focus area. Full ladder at <a href="/services/">/services</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="vert-engagements">
    <a href="/services/#audit" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">SYSTEM AUDIT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE WEEK · QUOTE ON SCOPE</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#sprint" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">BUILD SPRINT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE BUILD · QUOTE ON SCOPE</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#custom" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">CUSTOM BUILD</span><span class="when">MULTI-WORKFLOW · MILESTONE-PAID</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#retainer" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">OPS RETAINER</span><span class="when">MONTHLY · POST-ENGAGEMENT ONLY</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-cta reveal" style="text-align: center;">
    <p style="margin: 0;">Working on something AI-shaped? <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Send the problem →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
